ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE KOREA EXPRESSWAY CORPORATION ACT

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Korea Expressway Corporation Act and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Types of Shares, etc.)
Shares issued by Korea Expressway Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the “Corporation”) pursuant to Article 5 of the Korea Expressway Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the “Act”) shall be registered common shares, and share certificates shall be of eight denominations: one share, ten shares, 100 shares, 1,000 shares, 10,000 shares, 100,000 shares, one million shares and ten million shares.

Article 3 (Par Value and Total Number of Shares Issued)
The par value of each share issued by the Corporation shall be 10,000 won, and the total number of shares shall be the Corporation’s capital divided by the par value of each share.

Article 4 (Payment for Shares, etc.)
The timing of issuance, total number of shares issued, amount payable for shares, and timing and method of payment for shares other than shares subscribed for by the Government shall be as prescribed by the articles of incorporation.

Article 5 (Registration of Establishment)
(1) Registration of the Corporation’s establishment under Article 7 of the Act shall be completed within two weeks from the date on which the first payment of capital is made.
(2) The following matters shall be registered upon registration of establishment under paragraph (1):
1. Its purpose;
2. The name of the Corporation;
3. The location of its principal office;
4. The locations of its branches or offices;
5. Its capital;
6. The method of capital contribution and the amount paid in;
7. The name, resident registration number and address of its president;
8. The names and resident registration numbers of executive officers other than the president;
9. The method of public notice.

Article 6 (Registration of Establishment of Branches or Offices)
Where the Corporation establishes a branch or office, it shall register the name, location and date of establishment of the branch or office at the location of its principal office within two weeks after establishment.

Article 7 (Registration of Relocation)
(1) Where the Corporation relocates its principal office, it shall register the new location and date of relocation at the former or new location within two weeks after relocation.
(2) Where the Corporation relocates a branch or office, it shall register the new location and date of relocation at the location of its principal office within two weeks after relocation.

Article 8 (Registration of Changes)
Where a matter registered under any subparagraph of Article 5 (2) or under Article 6 changes (excluding cases constituting registration of relocation under Article 7), the Corporation shall register the change at the location of its principal office within two weeks after the change.

Article 9 (Registration of Appointment of Agents)
(1) Where the president appoints an agent pursuant to Article 11 of the Act, the Corporation shall register the following matters at the location of its principal office within two weeks after appointment. The same shall apply where a registered matter changes. <Amended on Jan. 21, 2025>
1. The name and address of the agent;
2. The name and location of the principal office, branch or office at which the agent is placed;
3. Where the agent’s authority is restricted, the details of the restriction.
(2) Where the president dismisses an agent appointed pursuant to Article 11 of the Act, the Corporation shall register that dismissal at the location of its principal office within two weeks after dismissal. <Amended on Jan. 21, 2025>

Article 10 (Documents Accompanying Applications for Registration)
An application for registration shall be accompanied by the following documents; provided, where information contained in accompanying documents can be confirmed through the shared use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act, such confirmation may substitute for the accompanying documents: <Amended on May 4, 2010>
1. For registration of establishment under Article 5: The articles of incorporation, documents proving subscription for shares and contributions in kind, documents proving payment for shares, and documents proving the qualifications of executive officers;
2. For registration of establishment of a branch or office under Article 6: Documents proving the relevant grounds and a certified copy of the register of the principal office;
3. For registrations under Articles 7 and 8: Documents proving the relevant grounds in each case;
4. For registration of appointment of an agent under Article 9: Documents proving that the appointment is pursuant to Article 11 of the Act and, where the agent’s authority is restricted pursuant to Article 9 (1) 3, documents proving the restriction.

Article 11 (Competent Registry Office)
Registration of the Corporation shall be handled by the district court, branch court or registry office having jurisdiction over the location of its principal office.

Article 11-2 (Business Activities Using Road Sites and Facilities)
The scope of business activities using road sites and facilities under Article 12 (1) 10 of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012>
1. Projects concerning the three-dimensional development of roads, such as the installation of business facilities, sales facilities or parking lots using road space;
2. Projects for the installation and management of transfer centers, complex transfer centers, parking lots, freight terminals, rest areas exclusively for freight vehicles, freight distribution and storage facilities, and sales facilities on road sites;
3. Advertising agency services using road structures;
4. Business activities providing private telecommunications facilities installed on roads to facilities-based telecommunications business operators (limited to provision pursuant to Article 21 (2) of the Framework Act on Telecommunications);
5. Business activities providing road traffic information collected using road facilities.

Article 11-3 (Development Projects in Areas Adjoining Roads)
(1) Areas adjoining toll roads under Article 12 (1) 11 of the Act shall be areas directly connected to toll roads for which the Corporation has obtained approval of a business plan from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
(2) The scope of business activities that the Corporation may carry out as development projects in areas adjoining roads shall be as follows: <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012>
1. Projects for the installation and management of passenger vehicle terminals, transfer centers, complex transfer centers, freight vehicle terminals, rest areas exclusively for freight vehicles, freight distribution and storage facilities, sales facilities, and other facilities necessary to improve the efficiency of motor vehicle traffic;
2. Projects for the installation and management of accommodation facilities, youth training facilities, sports facilities, social welfare facilities, cultural facilities, and other facilities to enhance the utility of roads and the convenience of users;
3. Logistics complex development projects under the Act on the Development and Operation of Logistics Facilities.
(3) Where seeking approval of a business plan for a development project in an area adjoining a road pursuant to Article 12 (2) of the Act, the Corporation shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for approval containing the following matters: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
1. The purpose of the project;
2. The area and scale of project implementation;
3. The project implementation period;
4. Project costs and financing plans;
5. Other matters necessary for project implementation.

Article 11-4 (Research and Technology Development)
(1) The Corporation shall include in its budget an amount of at least one percent of its toll revenue for each business year as expenditure for research and technology development concerning toll roads under Article 12 (1) 12 of the Act.
(2) Where intending to perform duties concerning research and technology development, the Corporation shall establish a business plan containing the following matters and obtain a resolution of the board of directors:
1. Matters concerning research and technology development tasks;
2. Matters concerning the amounts required for research and technology development and their use;
3. Other matters necessary for research and technology development.

Article 11-5 (Investments, etc.)
(1) Business activities in which the Corporation may invest or to which it may make contributions pursuant to Article 12 (1) 13 of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012>
1. Investigation, surveying, design, testing, supervision, research and technology development concerning roads;
2. Education, training and development of specialist personnel related to road affairs;
3. Maintenance of roads and road management facilities;
4. Leasing of equipment necessary for road construction and maintenance;
5. Business activities using road sites and facilities and development projects in areas adjoining roads that are undertaken to enhance the utility of toll roads and the convenience of users;
6. Telecommunications business activities using private telecommunications facilities installed on roads;
7. Road projects carried out as public-private partnership projects under the Act on Public-Private Partnerships in Infrastructure (limited to road projects falling within the Corporation’s duties);
8. Business activities concerning road construction, maintenance, investigation, design, supervision and construction project management overseas;
8-2. New and renewable energy power generation business activities under the Act on the Promotion of the Development, Use and Diffusion of New and Renewable Energy using sites and facilities managed by the Corporation;
9. Business activities that the Corporation may carry out under other statutes;
10. Business activities aimed at supporting those under subparagraphs 1 through 8, 8-2 and 9.
(2) Where intending to invest in or make contributions to business activities pursuant to paragraph (1), the Corporation shall obtain a resolution of the board of directors and then report to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 11-6 (Fees for Entrusted Duties)
Fees necessary to perform duties entrusted under Article 12-2 (2) of the Act shall be determined through consultation between the Corporation and the entrusted person.

Article 12 Deleted. <Aug. 31, 1999>

Article 13 (Exercise of Authority on Behalf of Authorities, etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 13 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may have the Corporation exercise on the Minister’s behalf the authority of road management authorities concerning roads prescribed in Articles 31 (1), 33 through 36, 40 through 44, 47 (2), 49, 55 through 57, 61 through 74, 76 through 78, 80 through 83, 89, 90, 91 (1), (2) and (4), 95 through 97, 98 (2) and (3), 99, 100, 102, 103, 106 (2) and 111 of the Road Act and Articles 43 and 44 (1) through (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the same Act. <Amended on Jul. 14, 2014>
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport has the Corporation exercise the Minister’s authority pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall give public notice of the route name and section of the relevant road, the details of the authority to be exercised on the Minister’s behalf, and the period for which that authority is to be exercised. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
(3) Where, pursuant to Article 13 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport has the Corporation carry out and manage, at its own expense, works for the new construction, reconstruction, maintenance and repair of a road designated for conversion into a toll road, the Minister shall attach a business plan to a written order stating the following matters: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
1. The type and route name of the road;
2. The sections for road construction and maintenance;
3. The periods for road construction and maintenance.
(4) Where having the Corporation exercise the authority of a road management authority pursuant to Article 13 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall obtain the consent of the relevant road management authority. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 13-2 (Entrustment of Authority for Administrative Vicarious Execution, etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 13-2 of the Act, the head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government shall entrust the following authority to the Corporation: <Amended on Jul. 27, 2009>
1. Administrative vicarious execution under Article 89 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects;
2. Removal of illegal facilities under Article 74 of the State Property Act.
(2) Where the Corporation has carried out administrative vicarious execution or removed illegal facilities pursuant to paragraph (1), it shall notify the head of the relevant central administrative agency or the head of the relevant local government of the results without delay.

Article 14 (Transfer of Earned Surplus Reserves to Capital, etc.)
(1) Transfer of earned surplus reserves to capital under Article 14 (3) of the Act shall be determined by the general meeting of shareholders.
(2) Use of the business expansion reserve under Article 14 (3) of the Act shall be prescribed by the Corporation’s articles of incorporation.

Article 15 (Issuance of Corporate Bonds)
(1) To issue corporate bonds pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act, the Corporation shall prepare the following matters and obtain a resolution of the board of directors: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
1. The purpose of issuing the corporate bonds;
2. The method and timing of issuance of the corporate bonds;
3. The total amount to be issued;
4. The amount for each type of corporate bond;
5. The interest rate;
6. The method and deadline for repayment of principal;
7. The method and deadline for payment of interest;
8. The method of placement.
(2) Corporate bond certificates shall state the following matters and bear the name and seal of the president:
1. The bond number;
2. The date of issuance;
3. The matters under paragraph (1) 4 through 7.

Article 16 (Subsidies, etc.)
(1) Subsidies under Article 16 (1) of the Act shall be paid in any of the following cases:
1. Where the Corporation newly constructs a toll road or reconstructs an existing road to convert it into a toll road;
2. Where a general national highway connected to a toll road managed by the Corporation is reconstructed to enhance the utility of that toll road.
(2) The State may have the Korea Development Bank provide loans of fiscal funds under Article 16 (1) of the Act.

Article 17 (Payment of Management Costs for Toll-Free National Expressways)
(1) Where seeking payment of costs for reconstruction, repair and maintenance of national expressways on which no tolls are collected pursuant to Article 16 (2) of the Act, the Corporation shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for payment, accompanied by a business plan stating the following matters, no later than 20 days before the beginning of the business year: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
1. The purpose of the project;
2. The route name;
3. The section and location;
4. The project period;
5. The amount required for the project.
(2) Upon receiving an application for payment under paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall review the business plan and pay the necessary costs within budgetary limits. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 17-2 (Bearing of Public Service Costs)
(1) Where having the State bear public service costs pursuant to Article 16-2 (1) of the Act, the Corporation shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an estimate of costs to be borne by the State, stating the estimated amount of public service costs that the State is to bear for the following year (hereinafter referred to as “State-borne costs”), the details of the relevant public service, and other necessary matters. In such cases, when calculating the estimated amount of State-borne costs, the Corporation shall consider compensation agreements, etc. under Article 16-3 (1) of the Act. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
(2) Upon receiving an estimate of State-borne costs under paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may, in consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies, include the State-borne costs in the accounts under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport for the following year. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
(3) When determining State-borne costs under paragraph (2), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall consider the estimated amount of State-borne costs under paragraph (1), the State-borne costs paid for the preceding year, relevant statutes, compensation agreements under Article 16-3 (1) of the Act, etc. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 17-3 (Payment of State-Borne Costs)
(1) When applying for payment of State-borne costs, the Corporation shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for payment of State-borne costs, accompanied by the following documents, within the period designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
1. The amount of State-borne costs for which payment is requested and a detailed calculation statement;
2. A detailed statement of expected revenue for the relevant year;
3. A detailed statement of State-borne costs received over the most recent two years.
(2) Upon receiving an application for payment of State-borne costs pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may review it and pay State-borne costs within budgetary limits. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 17-4 (Settlement of State-Borne Costs)
(1) The Corporation that has received State-borne costs pursuant to Article 17-3 (2) shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport a statement of settlement of State-borne costs, accompanied by the following documents, within 60 days after the end of the relevant half-year: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jan. 5, 2021>
1. A detailed statement of revenue and expenditure;
2. Other accounting-related documents, such as a statement of financial position.
(2) Upon receiving a statement of settlement of State-borne costs pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may have a specialized institution, etc. under Article 16-3 (4) of the Act check the statement of settlement. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 17-5 (Deliberative Body)
“Deliberative body prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 16-3 (5) of the Act means the Road Policy Deliberation Committee under Article 9 of the Road Act. <Amended on Jul. 14, 2014>

Article 17-6 (Documents Accompanying Applications for Approval of Restrictions on Public Services, etc.)
When submitting an application for approval to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport pursuant to Article 16-4 (2) of the Act, the Corporation shall attach documents stating the following matters: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
1. The reasons for applying for approval;
2. The status of reductions or exemptions, or details of costs, of the public service intended to be restricted or suspended;
3. The total amount of public service costs over the preceding two years and the amount of public service costs charged to the parties responsible for causing the costs pursuant to Article 16-2 (1) of the Act.

Article 17-7 (Fact-Finding Surveys)
(1) Upon receiving an application for approval under Article 16-4 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may conduct a fact-finding survey on the status of provision of the relevant public service. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
(2) Where necessary, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may have the relevant parties responsible for causing the costs or relevant specialized institutions participate in a fact-finding survey under paragraph (1). <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
(3) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall notify the deliberative body under Article 17-5 of the results of a fact-finding survey under paragraph (1). <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>
(4) When deliberating on a restriction or suspension of a public service through the deliberative body under Article 17-5, the relevant parties responsible for causing the costs may be invited to attend and present their opinions.

Article 17-8 (Public Notice of Restrictions on Public Services, etc.)
Where granting approval pursuant to Article 16-4 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall, within ten days from the date of approval, give public notice of the details of the public service to be restricted or suspended, the reasons therefor, the timing of the restriction or suspension, etc., as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013>

